## 1. GDS Provider API Analysis (Source of Truth)

### Two Servers
| Server | Base URL | Purpose |
|--------|----------|---------|
| Partner API | `https://partnerapi.iamgds.com/` | Auth, cities, search, chart, single-bus search |
| Transaction API | `https://partnertranapi.iamgds.com/` | Hold, book, booking status, cancel, booking details, balance |

### 12 Documented Endpoints

| # | Method | Path | Server | Purpose |
|---|--------|------|--------|---------|
| 1 | POST | `/ota/v1/Auth` | Partner | Get access token (90 min TTL) |
| 2 | GET | `/ota/CityList` | Partner | List all cities |
| 3 | GET | `/ota/Search` | Partner | Search buses by from/to/date |
| 4 | GET | `/ota/Chart` | Partner | Seat chart for a specific bus |
| 5 | GET | `/ota/SearchBus` | Partner | Single bus details |
| 6 | POST | `/ota/HoldSeats` | Transaction | Hold seats for user |
| 7 | POST | `/ota/BookSeats` | Transaction | Confirm booking after hold |
| 8 | POST | `/ota/bookingstatusv2` | Transaction | Check booking status by HoldId |
| 9 | GET | `/ota/IsCancellable` | Transaction | Check cancellation eligibility |
| 10 | POST | `/ota/CancelSeats` | Transaction | Cancel seats |
| 11 | GET | `/ota/BookingDetails` | Transaction | Get booking details by PNR+TicketNo |
| 12 | GET | `/ota/balance` | Transaction | Agent balance |

### Authentication
- **Credentials**: `ClientId` (int) + `ClientSecret` (string)
- **Response**: Raw string token (not JSON object)
- **TTL**: 90 minutes (doc says cache for 24h, but token valid 90 min)
- **Header**: Access token passed in headers for subsequent calls
- **Security**: ClientSecret must never leave server

### Key Provider Identifiers
| Identifier | Source | Usage |
|------------|--------|-------|
| `CityId` | CityList | Search from/to |
| `TripId` | Search | Format: `"{ProvId}:{RouteId}"` or `"{RouteId}"` |
| `RouteBusId` / `BusId` | Search/Chart | Identifies bus on a route |
| `ChartCode` | Search/Chart | Opaque chart identifier |
| `PickupCode` | Chart | Boarding point identifier |
| `DropoffCode` | Chart | Alighting point identifier |
| `HoldId` | HoldSeats | Links hold → book → status |
| `TicketNo` | BookSeats | Booking reference |
| `PNRNo` | BookSeats | Operator PNR for ticket |
| `seq_no` | Chart Layout | Maps to seat_no, fare, status via array index |

### Seat Status Codes (from Chart)
| Code | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| 0 | Not Available |
| 1 | Available for all |
| 2 | Available only for male |
| 3 | Available only for female |
| -2 | Booked by male |
| -3 | Booked by female |

### Seat Type IDs
| ID | Type |
|----|------|
| 1 | Seating |
| 2 | Sleeper |
| 4 | Semi Sleeper |

### Fare Array Structure
`[total_fare, base_fare, 0, 0, 0, 0]`
- `total_fare - base_fare` = applicable charges including service tax

### Cancellation Policy Structure
```json
{ "Amt": 0, "Pct": 10, "Mins": 600 }
```
- `Pct`: Cancellation charge percentage
- `Mins`: Minutes before departure when this policy applies
- `Amt`: Fixed cancellation amount (0 in examples)

### BookingStatus Response Codes
| Status | Meaning |
|--------|---------|
| 1 | Hold ID found, booking successful |
| 0 | Hold ID found, booking in progress |
| -1 | Hold ID found, booking unsuccessful/cancelled |
| -2 | Hold ID not found |

### CancelSeats Response
Returns `NewHoldId`, `NewTicketNo`, `NewPNRNo` — indicating the provider creates a new booking record for the post-cancellation state.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The GDS documentation does **not** specify: rate limits, error response format for failures (only success examples shown), webhook callbacks, hold TTL duration, maximum passengers per hold, or timeout behavior. These are marked as **unresolved integration points**.

